  {
    "page_number": 15,
    "blocks": [
      {
        "evidence_id": "ev_p15_b207",
        "type": "heading",
        "section_path": [],
        "bbox": [
          0.3611,
          0.066,
          0.6454,
          0.0787
        ],
        "text": "NASA-STD-8739.14 - 2020-06-02"
      },
      {
        "evidence_id": "ev_p15_b208",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "section_path": [],
        "bbox": [
          0.1765,
          0.0984,
          0.8653,
          0.1289
        ],
        "text": "Energy Dispersive Spectroscopy (EDS), and may be used to verify the correct alloy but do not provide a sufficient level of accuracy to satisfy this requirement."
      },
      {
        "evidence_id": "ev_p15_b209",
        "type": "heading",
        "section_path": [],
        "bbox": [
          0.1177,
          0.1485,
          0.3175,
          0.1615
        ],
        "text": "4.5.8 Tensile Testing"
      },
      {
        "evidence_id": "ev_p15_b210",
        "type": "list",
        "section_path": [],
        "bbox": [
          0.2281,
          0.181,
          0.8862,
          0.2289
        ],
        "text": "Tensile testing shall be performed on a sampling basis for level II threaded fasteners such as bolts, screws, nuts, and nut plates that have been procured from a nonqualified suppliers or have incomplete traceability."
      },
      {
        "evidence_id": "ev_p15_b211",
        "type": "list",
        "section_path": [],
        "bbox": [
          0.2281,
          0.2485,
          0.8834,
          0.2789
        ],
        "text": "Tensile testing shall be performed in accordance with one of the following standards:"
      },
      {
        "evidence_id": "ev_p15_b212",
        "type": "list",
        "section_path": [],
        "bbox": [
          0.1471,
          0.2982,
          0.7719,
          0.3134
        ],
        "text": "NASM1312-8, Fastener Test Methods, Method 8, Tensile Strength -Rev 2"
      },
      {
        "evidence_id": "ev_p15_b213",
        "type": "list",
        "section_path": [],
        "bbox": [
          0.1471,
          0.3319,
          0.8623,
          0.347
        ],
        "text": "NAM1312-108, Fastener Test Methods, Metric, Method 108, Tensile Strength -Rev 1"
      },
      {
        "evidence_id": "ev_p15_b214",
        "type": "list",
        "section_path": [],
        "bbox": [
          0.1471,
          0.3658,
          0.8189,
          0.4137
        ],
        "text": "ASTM F606/F606M-16, Standard Test Methods for Determining the Mechanical Properties of Externally and Internally Threaded Fasteners, Washers, Direct Tension Indicators, and Rivets"
      },
      {
        "evidence_id": "ev_p15_b215",
        "type": "list",
        "section_path": [],
        "bbox": [
          0.2281,
          0.4332,
          0.8414,
          0.4637
        ],
        "text": "Tensile test reports shall identify the location of the tensile break, the ultimate load/strength, and the specification minimum and maximum values."
      },
      {
        "evidence_id": "ev_p15_b216",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "section_path": [],
        "bbox": [
          0.1765,
          0.4832,
          0.8697,
          0.5485
        ],
        "text": "Note: Load extension curves are not required. Level II fasteners that are smaller than #10 or shorter than 2 times their diameter may need to be procured through a qualified supplier with complete traceability, since tensile testing at receiving inspection may not be possible."
      },
      {
        "evidence_id": "ev_p15_b217",
        "type": "heading",
        "section_path": [],
        "bbox": [
          0.1177,
          0.5686,
          0.4822,
          0.5814
        ],
        "text": "4.6 Handling, Packaging, and Storage"
      },
      {
        "evidence_id": "ev_p15_b218",
        "type": "list",
        "section_path": [],
        "bbox": [
          0.1177,
          0.6032,
          0.8845,
          0.6337
        ],
        "text": "Fasteners shall be handled, packaged, and stored in a manner designed to prevent damage.  This will include environmental controls for temperature, humidity, and contamination."
      },
      {
        "evidence_id": "ev_p15_b219",
        "type": "list",
        "section_path": [],
        "bbox": [
          0.1177,
          0.6532,
          0.8329,
          0.6837
        ],
        "text": "Fasteners shall be handled, packaged, and stored in a manner designed to prevent commingling of lots."
      },
      {
        "evidence_id": "ev_p15_b220",
        "type": "list",
        "section_path": [],
        "bbox": [
          0.1177,
          0.7032,
          0.7576,
          0.7163
        ],
        "text": "Fasteners shall be stored in a controlled access area until issued for use."
      },
      {
        "evidence_id": "ev_p15_b221",
        "type": "list",
        "section_path": [],
        "bbox": [
          0.1177,
          0.7358,
          0.5387,
          0.7488
        ],
        "text": "Fastener documentation shall be controlled."
      },
      {
        "evidence_id": "ev_p15_b222",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "section_path": [],
        "bbox": [
          0.1765,
          0.7684,
          0.8122,
          0.7989
        ],
        "text": "Note: it is recommended that external packaging marking includes part number, lot number, and supplier name."
      },
      {
        "evidence_id": "ev_p15_b223",
        "type": "footer",
        "section_path": [],
        "bbox": [
          0.4458,
